A. Create a Jira Cloud Account & Explore the Dashboard
Go to the Atlassian Jira sign-up page (atlassian.com/software/jira).

Click Get it free.

Sign up using your email address, Google account, or Microsoft account.

Enter a site name for your workspace (e.g., yourcompany.atlassian.net) and click Agree and sign up.

Follow the quick onboarding setup prompts (or click Skip).

Explore the main dashboard layout:

Top Bar: Search, notifications, help center, and global settings (gear icon).

Left Navigation: Recent projects, filters, dashboards, and teams.

Main Area: Recent work, assigned tasks, and quick activity feeds.

B. Create a Company-Managed Scrum/Kanban Project
Click Projects in the top navigation bar.

Select Create project.

Choose a project template: select either Scrum or Kanban.

Click Use template.

Choose Company-managed project as the project type.

C. Configure Project Details
Enter a Name for your project (e.g., Software Development).

Verify or edit the generated Key (a short 2–10 letter prefix used for issue IDs, e.g., SD).

Click Create project.

To configure details further, click Project settings at the bottom of the left sidebar.

In Details, set or edit:

Project Description: Short summary of the project.

Project Lead: The team member responsible for managing the project.

Default Assignee: Person assigned to new issues automatically (e.g., Project Lead or Unassigned).

Project Avatar/Icon: Custom image for visual identification.

Click Save changes.
